{
  "info": {
    "name": "Sygnal — UC3 Downward Task-out (ComEMR → DIGIT HCM)",
    "_postman_id": "2cd4d339-a696-5522-8d5d-6821b9fa47be",
    "description": "### Quick-start: environment setup\n\n1. Import this use case's **`*_Dev.postman_environment.json`** (in the same\n   `reference-flows/` folder) into Postman (Environments → Import). Each use case\n   ships a self-contained environment — Postman allows only one active environment\n   at a time, so per-UC envs avoid one ever-growing shared file.\n2. Select that environment from the picker.\n3. Set `bpp_uri`, `bap_uri`, and `auth_token` for your sandbox. `bpp_uri` is the target\n   base URL and switches by transaction (ComEMR for T1, HCM for UC3, CARE for UC4-T2).\n4. `network_id` is `example.net/health` (STUB) — confirm with the registry team.\n5. Subscriber IDs (`hcm_np_id`, `comemr_np_id`, `care_np_id`) and all keys are STUBBED.\n\n**Envelope note:** `context.version` is `2.0.0` — the Beckn *core message* version (a\nconst in beckn.yaml). The domain schema packs (HealthReferral / ServiceCoordination)\nare v2.1; that shows up in the `@context` URLs, not the envelope.\n\n## Sygnal — UC3 · Downward Task-out (ComEMR → DIGIT HCM)\n\n**Scenario:** ComEMR needs field checks / data collection performed by a campaign-mode CHW.\nIt discovers a suitable campaign, then contracts the task.\n\n**Roles:** BAP = ComEMR (seeker). BPP = DIGIT HCM (provider offering campaign field capacity).\n\n**Matched transaction:** discover → on_discover → select → init → confirm → on_confirm → status → update.\n\n**Payload:** the **generic `ServiceCoordination`** contract (not `HealthReferral`) — a field\ntask has no clinical specialty/urgency/referral-note, so the generic base is the correct fit.\n`targetCriteria.serviceCategory` = `FIELD_DATA_COLLECTION`, a **self-authored** `ServiceCategory`\nCodedValue (permitted by the schema's self-owned CodedValue design).\n\n**Data path:** collected clinical data travels via the records/HIE layer — only task metadata\nand completion state are on-network.\n\n### ⚠ Schema gap — consent on the generic contract\nThe generic `ServiceContract` / `ServiceCoordination` / `ServiceParticipant` pack has **no\nconsent field**. Consent (`hrf:consent`) exists only in the health pack. UC3's class-A consent\nis therefore carried here as a **self-authored extension object** on the generic\n`contractAttributes`, mirroring the `hrf:consent` shape. To standardise, either add a generic\n`consent` field to `ServiceContract` or bind consent via `ServiceConsideration`.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
